The common backbone idea in the provided algorithms is to prioritize bins where adding the item leads to a more efficient or compact utilization of space, with a focus on minimizing leftover capacity or maximizing the relative use of available space, while ensuring feasibility.
}

{
New algorithm: For each bin, compute the remaining capacity after hypothetically adding the item, then assign higher priority to bins where the remaining capacity is minimized (closest to zero without going negative), and among those, break ties by preferring bins with larger original capacity.
}

{
Assign priority based on the ratio of the item size to the bin capacity, preferring bins where the item fills a larger proportion of the remaining space, and penalize infeasible bins.
}
